---
import "@fontsource-variable/geist";
import "@fontsource-variable/geist-mono";
import "../styles/site.css";
import Demo from "../components/Demo.astro";
import demo from "../data/demo.json";
import test from "../data/test_step.json";

const EMAIL = "shivansh@lockwirerobotics.com";
const ASK = "mailto:" + EMAIL + "?subject=" + encodeURIComponent("48-hour check");
const GITHUB = "https://github.com/Shivansh2703/lockwire";

// Every number below is read from the data files.
const plan = demo.plan;
const zKey = "Accelerometer Z";
const z = test.outside_pct[zKey];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <title>Lockwire · Find out your robot won't work before you buy the parts</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Lockwire checks that the numbers from every datasheet in your robot add up, then checks the powered robot against them. See it catch a real overloaded rail on a real drone design." />
  <meta property="og:title" content="Lockwire" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Find out your robot won't work before you buy the parts." />
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://lockwirerobotics.com/og.png" />
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://lockwirerobotics.com/" />
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://lockwirerobotics.com/" />
</head>
<body>
  <header class="nav wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Lockwire home"><img src="/favicon.svg" alt="" width="24" height="24" />lockwire</a>
    <nav>
      <a href="#catches">What it catches</a>
      <a href="#plans">Plans</a>
      <a href={GITHUB}>GitHub</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <h1>Find out your robot won't work before you buy the parts.</h1>
      <p class="sub">Every robot is a stack of numbers from a dozen datasheets. Lockwire checks that they add up while you plan, then checks the powered robot against them.</p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href={ASK}>Get a 48-hour check</a>
        <a class="quiet" href={GITHUB}>Try it free on GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <Demo />

    <section id="catches" class="wrap section">
      <h2>What it catches</h2>
      <div class="tablewrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>How Lockwire knows</th><th>On the drone above</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {plan.check.violations.map((x) => (
              <tr><td>{x.quantity.endsWith("7w-mode") ? "Overloaded even in low-power mode" : "Overloaded power rail"}</td><td>Adds every part's draw on a rail and compares it with what the supply can give</td><td class="num">{x.observed.split(" (")[0]} on {x.expected.replace("<= ", "")} · <span class="badtext">{x.delta.match(/\(([^)]+)\)/)?.[1]}</span></td></tr>
            ))}
            <tr><td>Missing numbers</td><td>Names every value it could not check, so a gap is never a silent pass</td><td class="num">{plan.check.counts.not_scored} not checked, each named</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sensors drifting after power-on</td><td>Learns each sensor's normal range from known-good runs, then flags readings outside it</td><td class="num">{zKey}: {z.known_good}% → <span class="badtext">{z.checked}%</span> out of range</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="plans" class="wrap section">
      <h2>Plans</h2>
      <div class="plans">
        <div class="plan">
          <h3>Lockwire Free</h3>
          <p class="planline">Open source. Plan and check a robot yourself.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The check: power, mass and bus budgets</li>
            <li>Command line and Python library</li>
            <li>Desktop app for macOS and Linux</li>
            <li>GitHub Action for CI</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="quiet" href={GITHUB}>Try it free on GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <div class="plan">
          <h3>Lockwire Pro</h3>
          <p class="planline">For teams with a robot on the bench.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Everything in Free</li>
            <li>The go/no-go gate on the powered robot</li>
            <li>Known-good baselines and drift checks</li>
            <li>ROS 2 bags and PX4 flight logs</li>
            <li>Set up with you on your own robot</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="quiet" href={ASK}>Get a 48-hour check</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section ask">
      <h2>Send us your parts list or URDF.</h2>
      <p>Within 48 hours you get back the numbers that don't add up.</p>
      <p class="actions"><a class="btn" href={ASK}>Get a 48-hour check</a> <a class="quiet" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="wrap foot">
    <span>© 2026 Lockwire</span>
    <span><a href={GITHUB}>GitHub</a> · <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></span>
    <span class="credits">Drone model: <a href={GITHUB}>lockwire</a>, Apache-2.0. Test data: <a href="https://review.px4.io/">PX4 Flight Review</a>, CC BY 4.0.</span>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
